  cites Safari chapter Safari
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 Safari: the whole ride, one frame at a time.

 THE ORDER INSIDE THE STEP IS THE WHOLE CONTENT. The rider moves first and the
 truck steps against his NEW route distance, because the chase schedule anchors
 to where he is now -- stepping it against the old distance would leave the lead
 one frame stale at exactly the moments it is tightest. That is graded directly:
 the truck's answer after a step is what `truck-next` gives for the NEW distance
 and not for the old one, and on a moving rider those two differ.

 THE FINISH RESTARTS THE RIDE RATHER THAN STOPPING IT, because this is a
 screensaver. A finished rider is replaced by the initial ride whole -- rider,
 truck and clock together -- so the clock going back to zero is the observable
 and it is the one a chapter that merely reset the rider would fail.

 THE CLOCK IS A FRAME COUNT AND NOTHING READS IT AS TIME, so it is graded for the
 one property it has: it goes up by exactly one per step, and back to zero at the
 restart.

 We say:

Section: The Start

  segs : List Segment
  segs = seg-list 0

  seg-list : Integer -> List Segment
  seg-list (i) = if i >= list-length route then [] else [segment-at i] & seg-list (i + 1)

  start-got : List Real
  start-got =
    [ ride-initial.clock,
      ride-initial.rider.along,
      ride-initial.rider.across,
      ride-initial.rider.v,
      ride-initial.truck.pos,
      ride-initial.truck.v ]

  start-want : List Real
  start-want = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.3, 500.0, 0.3]

  start-index-got : List Integer
  start-index-got = [ride-initial.rider.segment]

  start-index-want : List Integer
  start-index-want = [0]

  start-flag-got : List Boolean
  start-flag-got = [ride-initial.truck.braking, is-finished ride-initial.rider segs]

  start-flag-want : List Boolean
  start-flag-want = [False, False]

Section: One Step

 The rider moves, the truck moves, the clock ticks once.

  one : Ride
  one = ride-next segs ride-initial

  two : Ride
  two = ride-next segs one

  step-got : List Real
  step-got = [one.clock, two.clock, two.clock - one.clock]

  step-want : List Real
  step-want = [1.0, 2.0, 1.0]

  moved-got : List Boolean
  moved-got =
    [ one.rider.along > ride-initial.rider.along,
      one.truck.pos > ride-initial.truck.pos,
      two.rider.along > one.rider.along ]

  moved-want : List Boolean
  moved-want = [True, True, True]

 THE TRUCK STEPS AGAINST THE RIDER'S NEW DISTANCE. Both candidates are computed
 here: the step matches the one taken against the NEW distance, and the two are
 required to DIFFER -- which is what makes this an assertion rather than a
 restatement. They differ for a reason worth knowing: at the start the truck sits
 exactly on the schedule, so a rider who has not moved leaves it holding speed
 while a rider who has moved puts it a fraction behind and it accelerates.

  order-got : List Boolean
  order-got =
    let old-dist = route-distance segs ride-initial.rider.segment ride-initial.rider.along
    in let new-dist = route-distance segs one.rider.segment one.rider.along
    in let against-new = truck-next ride-initial.truck new-dist segs (course-length segs)
    in let against-old = truck-next ride-initial.truck old-dist segs (course-length segs)
    in [ one.truck.pos ~0 against-new.pos,
         new-dist > old-dist,
         (against-new.pos ~0 against-old.pos) == False ]

  order-want : List Boolean
  order-want = [True, True, True]

Section: The Restart

 A finished rider is replaced by the initial ride WHOLE -- rider, truck and clock
 -- so the clock going back to zero is the observable.

  done : Ride
  done =
    Ride { rider = RiderState { segment = 18, along = 400.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = 0.0,
                                tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.9 },
           truck = TruckState { pos = 9000.0, v = 2.0, braking = True },
           clock = 12345.0 }

  restart-got : List Real
  restart-got =
    let r = ride-next segs done
    in [r.clock, r.rider.along, r.rider.v, r.truck.pos, r.rider.focus]

  restart-want : List Real
  restart-want = [0.0, 0.0, 0.3, 500.0, 0.0]

  restart-flag-got : List Boolean
  restart-flag-got = [is-finished done.rider segs, (ride-next segs done).truck.braking]

  restart-flag-want : List Boolean
  restart-flag-want = [True, False]

 A ride that is NOT finished steps instead, which is the other arm of the same
 test.

  not-done-got : List Boolean
  not-done-got = [one.clock > 0.0, is-finished one.rider segs == False]

  not-done-want : List Boolean
  not-done-want = [True, True]

Section: The Frame

 A frame is the backdrop, then the floor, then everything that stands up -- so it
 is never empty, and every command carries a tag the blitter knows.

  frame : List DrawCmd
  frame = ride-frame segs ride-initial

  frame-got : List Boolean
  frame-got =
    [ list-length frame > 0,
      list-length (ride-frame segs one) > 0,
      (list-at frame 0).tag >= 0,
      (list-at frame 0).tag <= 6 ]

  frame-want : List Boolean
  frame-want = [True, True, True, True]

 The sun is placed for the ride's own clock, and at the start it is up.

  sun-got : List Boolean
  sun-got =
    let s = ride-sun segs ride-initial
    in [s.visible == False, s.scale >= 0.0]

  sun-want : List Boolean
  sun-want = [True, True]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "sf-start " start-got start-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "sf-sindex" start-index-got start-index-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sf-sflag " start-flag-got start-flag-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "sf-step  " step-got step-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sf-moved " moved-got moved-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sf-order " order-got order-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "sf-restrt" restart-got restart-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sf-rflag " restart-flag-got restart-flag-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sf-notdon" not-done-got not-done-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sf-frame " frame-got frame-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sf-sun   " sun-got sun-want)
  end
